+# Write amplification: the same bytes, fewer calls
+
+A record of a 64-byte payload costs 72 bytes in the log — four for its length, four for the
+[seal](../src/engine/wal/segment.rs) over both — and that arithmetic belongs to the format, not to
+the write path. What the write path decides is how many times it asks the kernel to do something
+about those bytes, and the shape it has had since `lakelet/4.1-ingest-protocol` is *twice per
+record*: one open and one write inside [`Spool::append`](../src/engine/spool.rs), plus one device
+call per record under a policy that waits.
+
